From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:22:38 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Bug XXXXXXX - Offer credential portal passkeys in
 WebAuthn autofill on Linux. r?mfarrell

Conditional mediation needs the list of credentials for a site without
user interaction. A platform authenticator behind the credential portal
can give that list (user name and credential ID only, no signature), so
ask the portal with ListConditional, which takes the same origin and
options as GetCredential and returns an aa{sv} of credentials with "id"
and "user_name". The portal reports whether it supports this through its
ConditionalGet property, which now feeds the conditionalGet capability.

WebAuthnService passes the request's args to the portal service for this,
since GetAutoFillEntriesForRpId has only the RP ID and the portal checks
the origin. When the user picks an entry, the promoted request carries
only that credential in its allow list, so the request JSON sent to
GetCredential is narrowed to match.

ListConditional is not in the portal yet; it is proposed alongside this
patch. Without it the call fails and autofill shows no portal entries.
